    refuses those with no --force (wq#582), so an orchestrator directed to build one had no way
    to record intent before this. Allowed on ANY status='open' ticket (deps met or not); NOT a
    claim, acquires no lease/subsystem locks. Only the holder (or an expired hold) may re-hold or
    claim over it — see the hold_by check in cmd_claim's _eligible(). Cleared by claim/done/
    release; otherwise expires on its own after --ttl minutes."""
    ping("hold")
    agent, _ = resolve_identity(a)
    c = conn(); c.isolation_level = None
    c.execute("BEGIN IMMEDIATE")
    t_now = now()
    row = c.execute("SELECT id, lane, status, hold_by, hold_expires FROM tasks WHERE id=?",
                     (a.id,)).fetchone()
